<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Shell xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
       xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
       x:Class="MALPlus.AppShell"
       Shell.NavBarIsVisible="False"
       Shell.TabBarIsVisible="False">
    <!--
      The item / section / content tree is built in AppShell.xaml.cs, not here.

      MAUI 11 RC1's XAML generator emits `section.Items = ...` for the children of a
      ShellSection, but Items is get-only, so any XAML that puts more than one
      ShellContent inside a ShellSection fails to compile (CS0200). Doing it in code
      is both correct and required.

      The structure matters for behaviour: the four root sections must be four
      ShellContent inside ONE ShellSection. As four ShellContents under a TabBar MAUI
      produced four ShellItems instead, which land in shellitem_viewpager, whose
      renderer animates every switch and draws two full pages side by side (their
      BottomNavBars included). Here they live in shellsection_viewpager, whose renderer
      switches with SetCurrentItem(position, false), i.e. instantly.

      Routes are unchanged: //anime, //manga, //discover, //more.
    -->
</Shell>
